. 
. * ---------------------------------------------------------------
. * What if an effect did not operate? 'estat mems' switches one
. * coefficient off and compares a network summary that you define.
. * ---------------------------------------------------------------
. capture program drop mutualties

. program define mutualties, rclass
  1.     args netname
  2.     nwtomata `netname', mat(MM)
  3.     mata: st_numscalar("__mut", sum(MM :* MM') / 2)
  4.     return scalar stat = scalar(__mut)
  5. end

. quietly nwsaom, waves(glasgow1 glasgow2) outdegree reciprocity transtrip seed(4)

. estat mems, effect(reciprocity) macro(mutualties) nsim(100) seed(1)
interval 0: ..
interval 1: ..
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
MEMs (Micro Effects on Macro Structure) - Duxbury, via mutualties
Micro process: reciprocity  Interval: 0 1  nsim: 100
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
|             Estimate    Std. Dev.    [95% CI]              MC p-val
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
MEMS           37.1800     11.4216      14.4250 ,  59.0000   0.0000
Prop. Change in M                        0.9742
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
(MEMS = mean difference in mutualties between interval=1 and interval=0; Prop. Change in M = that di
> fference as a proportion of the interval=1 value; MC p-val = proportion of draws with the opposite
>  sign - a real, disclosed simplification vs real netmediate/RSiena: independent simulation randomn
> ess per draw, no common-random-numbers pairing, and the VanderWeele E-value sensitivity bound is n
> ot yet implemented)
